From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Subject: [PATCH] flow: REPAIR_TIMING_MAX_ITERATIONS caps repair_timing
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

repair_timing takes -max_iterations, and the flow's repair_timing_helper
had no way to pass it. On a large block the setup repair of
TNS_END_PERCENT's endpoints can stop improving the worst slack long
before it has visited them all and then run for hours: XiangShan's
XSTile parent macro held its reg2reg WNS at -835.6 ps from iteration
1,610 to 1,990, at about 1,200 iterations an hour, at global route.

Empty, the default, sets no cap, as before.

Not upstreamed; retires at a bump onto an ORFS that carries it.

---
