+| <a name="REPAIR_TIMING_MAX_ITERATIONS"></a>REPAIR_TIMING_MAX_ITERATIONS| Cap every repair_timing call of the flow's stages at this many iterations (repair_timing -max_iterations). Empty, the default, sets no cap. On a large block the setup repair of TNS_END_PERCENT's endpoints can stop improving the worst slack long before it has visited them all, and then runs for hours: XiangShan's XSTile parent macro held its reg2reg WNS flat from iteration 1,610 to 1,990 at 1,200 iterations an hour.| |
 | <a name="REPAIR_TIMING_PATH_GROUP"></a>REPAIR_TIMING_PATH_GROUP| Restrict every repair_timing call of the flow's stages to one path group, reg2reg, in2reg, reg2out or in2out (repair_timing -path_group). Empty, the default, repairs every group. A block whose ports carry budgets no repair can meet (a parent macro whose ports are its blocks' pins) otherwise spends TNS_END_PERCENT's endpoints on its boundary paths and leaves its register-to-register paths, the ones that set its period, unrepaired.| |
